# Deployment

**Status:** Draft — founder review required
**Phase:** 6 — Engineering

## Purpose

Defines how GrantAI actually gets deployed and, critically, how Grant
Hunter's schedule is implemented — the piece every prior phase has referred
to but deferred to here.

## Deployment Pattern

Follows the existing BAE pattern: Lovable-built frontend, Supabase backend,
deployed via the standard portfolio pipeline. No new infrastructure
pattern introduced for this module.

## Grant Hunter's Trigger Mechanism

Recommend a GitHub Actions scheduled workflow, mirroring the existing
`sync-agents.yml` pattern already used elsewhere in the BAE portfolio for
propagation jobs — same tooling, different job:

```yaml
name: grant-hunter-sweep
on:
  schedule:
    - cron: "0 13 * * *"   # daily, adjust per FundingOrganizations.md cadence
  workflow_dispatch: {}     # allows manual trigger, matching GrantHunter-Agent.md
jobs:
  sweep:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Trigger Hunter run
        run: |
          curl -X POST "$HUNTER_RUN_ENDPOINT" \
            -H "Authorization: Bearer ${{ secrets.SERVICE_ROLE_KEY }}"
```

This hits the `POST /hunter/run` endpoint defined in `API.md` using the
service-role credential — the same credential that's structurally barred
from Tier 4 actions per `Security.md`, so even a misconfigured or
compromised workflow run can't submit anything on its own.

## Environments

- **Production** — real sources, real business profile data, real drafts
- **Test** — separate Supabase branch/project per `Testing.md`, used for
  Hunter dry runs and CI

## Cadence Note

The cron schedule above should match the "Update cadence" column already
recorded per-source in `FundingOrganizations.md` rather than running every
source at the same frequency — daily for Federal/State, weekly (or a
separate workflow) for Corporate/Foundation once those categories have
approved sources.

